# =============================================================================
# Local Vite / SPA (committed as example only — copy to `.env.local` / `.env`)
# =============================================================================
# Created/updated by `bunx convex dev` into `.env.local`:
#   CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:your-deployment-name
#   VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://….convex.cloud
#   VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL=https://….convex.site

# Optional: show email/password UI on `src/routes/_public/login.tsx`.
# Requires adding a Password provider in `convex/auth.ts` (Google-only by default).
# VITE_AUTH_PASSWORD_ENABLED=true

# Optional client-side labels (not read by Convex Auth — OAuth secrets go on the
# Convex deployment; see README).
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_NAME=

# =============================================================================
# Convex deployment env (set with `bunx convex env set KEY value`, NOT in Vite)
# =============================================================================
# From `bunx @convex-dev/auth` (dev frontend origin, JWT signing):
#   SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173
#   JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=…
#   JWKS=…
#
# Google OAuth (Auth.js / @convex-dev/auth reads these names exactly):
#   AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=….apps.googleusercontent.com
#   AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=…
#
# Convex also provides CONVEX_SITE_URL on the deployment (HTTP Actions URL).
# OAuth redirect URI in Google Cloud Console must be:
#   {CONVEX_SITE_URL}/api/auth/callback/google
#
# Production: re-run `bunx @convex-dev/auth --prod` and set AUTH_GOOGLE_* on prod.
